# PHASE 55 CLOSED: the escape claims over one corpus (escape-claims/check.py
# says what is asserted). Budgets follow 25-escape-analysis.md §5: unlimited on
# the fixture and bootstrap, bounded on the two big bundles, where every frame
# pop otherwise costs a full mark.
# The fixture is three files concatenated byte for byte, so the complete
# JavaScript source bytes and allocation identities are what expected.txt
# names; --strict is the stopped-clock guard and the snapshot, which only the
# fixture - calling every one of its confined sites - can carry.
# RUN: cat %S/fixture/contents.js %S/fixture/primitives.js %S/fixture/escapes.js > %t.js
# RUN: python3 %S/check.py --oracle ctcompile-test-type-oracle --claims ctcompile-test-escape-claims --script %{monorepo}/tools/check/escape-oracle.py --corpus %t.js --work %t --name fixture --strict
